# Data and Calculations

Spec: `docs/context/DATA_SPEC.md`.

## Quality gate

Assign `VALID`, `DEGRADED`, `STALE` or `INVALID` with reason codes. Thresholds
are per strategy and per timeframe. There is no single universal freshness
threshold; do not invent one.

## Canonical events

Every event records provider and instrument identity, event/source/receive
times, provider sequence, explicit units and precision, a raw payload
reference, and the normalization version. Corrections and duplicates are
explicit states, not silent overwrites.

## Calculation rules

- Event-time processing. Provisional and final bars are different states.
- No silent forward-fill for execution-critical data.
- Explicit period, annualization, currency, contracts/lots and percent/fraction
  units. Record model, convergence and calculation version.
- Layer 1 owns bars, returns, indicators, realized vol, IV, Greeks, skew, term
  structure, liquidity and OFI. It does not select or size trades.

## Replay integrity

Point-in-time universe and reference data. No completed bar used before
completion, no revised value used before publication. Same snapshot, config and
code version reproduces the same decision, byte for byte.

Raw and canonical data are preserved separately and immutably.
